            My help must come from thee.

All my hopes are fixed upon the Father’s only Son;
Jesus is my Savior, is he yours?
Hid with Christ in God abiding, till my work is done;
Jesus is my Savior, is he yours?

From the love and pow’r of evil he gives full release;
Jesus is my Savior, is he yours?
To my troubled spirit he hath given perfect peace;
Jesus is my Savior, is he yours?

With my Lord beside me there’s no room for doubt or fear;
Jesus is my Savior, is he yours?
In the hour of pain and trial he is ever near;
Jesus is my Savior, is he yours?

It is nearer to-day than before;
And our path is growing brighter day by day;
We shall soon reach that heavenly shore;
Let us sing, and watch, and pray.

Some one is called by the Lord,
Called to proclaim His great word;
Called now to tell of His wonderful grace,
How on the cross He once died in our place;
Called to be filled with the pow’r from on high,
Is it I? Is it I?

Some one is called now to go,
Out in the mist of life’s woe;
Out now to save those who wander from home,
Out just to bid them to Jesus now come;
Called to be filled with the pow’r from on high,
Is it I? Is it I?

Some one is called to be true,
God’s holy will now to do;
Called now to count earthly glory but dross,
Called every talent to lay at the cross;
There to be filled with the pow’r from on high,
Is it I? Is it I?

Just as of yore He on trial is standing,
Denied by the many and loved by the few;
Someone “Away with Him!” still is demanding;
My Lord, is it I? My friend, is it you?

Someone is crossing the deadline, dividing
The old life of sin and of shame from the new;
Someone just now is for Jesus deciding;
My Lord, is it I? My friend, is it you?

when I am tempted, to Jesus I go;
Is it not wonderful?
Strength He doth give me to conquer each foe;
