I have not found such a friend anywhere;
Is it not wonderful?
He never leaves me lest I should despair;
Is it not wonderful?

I do not ask for the pride of earth,
For the pride of wealth or the pride of birth;
Be this, the rather, my one great care;
In the Book of Life, that my name is there.

In the Lamb's book of life, that is kept in heaven,
Are written the names of those forgiven;
Is my name written there?

As woods, when shaken by the breeze,
Take deeper, firmer root;
As winter's frost but makes the trees
Abound in summer fruit;

Oh, the Cross has wondrous glory!
Oft I've proved this to be true;
When I'm in the way so narrow
I can see a pathway through;
And now sweetly Jesus whispers;
Take the Cross, thou need'st not fear,
For I've tried this way before thee,
